Preserve ADR-001 and the following rules throughout every milestone:\
\
1. Capabilities ship with the app; large model weights do not.\
2. Model installation requires explicit user consent.\
3. The app owns semantic intent and prompt profiles.\
4. A runtime owns transport and execution, not semantic rewriting.\
5. Provider identity is independent of backend identity.\
6. No local failure silently becomes a cloud request.\
7. Requested and resolved identities remain separately visible.\
8. Generation and embedding packs remain distinct.\
9. Shell/platform adapters own effects:\
     network, downloads, files, secure credentials, OS model APIs,\
     inference handles, drivers, and platform lifecycle.\
10. Rust owns deterministic:\
     identity, selection, validation, state transitions, readiness,\
     integrity, conformance policy, and provenance.\
11. A provider credential never enters Rust snapshots or Git.\
12. Raw recordings, transcripts, prompts, and reflective logs never enter CI.\
13. No target is called supported merely because it compiles.\
