Required property laws:\
\
Idempotence:\
  - resolving identical provider input twice yields identical identity;\
  - verifying identical inventory twice yields the same receipt;\
  - publishing twice creates no duplicate installation;\
  - installing the exact already-active variant creates no duplicate;\
  - removing an already-absent pack remains absent;\
  - indexing the same content hash + embedding identity creates one entry.\
\
Time-origin equivariance:\
  Shift every monotonic timestamp by constant \uc0\u916 .\
  Phase sequence, elapsed durations, stale decisions, and retry decisions\
  must remain equivalent.\
\
Window-shift equivariance:\
  Shift an indexed recording window by N samples.\
  Event ranges shift by N while event type and detector parameters remain fixed.\
\
Channel-permutation equivariance:\
  Permute values and matching electrode labels together.\
  Channel-associated outputs permute correspondingly.\
  Permuting values without labels must be rejected.\
\
Path invariance:\
  Moving a verified pack under a different private filesystem root does not\
  change its content or model identity.\
\
Artifact-order invariance:\
  Reordering declared artifacts does not change canonical manifest digests.\
\
Non-invariances:\
  Changing tokenizer, model revision, quantization, prompt profile,\
  embedding dimensions, pooling, normalization, task instruction,\
  channel identity, or numerical contract must change identity.\
\
Backend semantic conformance:\
  Do not require byte-identical stochastic prose across CUDA, Vulkan,\
  OpenVINO, QNN, Metal, or CPU.\
\
  Require:\
    - same model/tokenizer/template identity;\
    - exact prompt bytes;\
    - exact input token IDs;\
    - exact stop-token configuration;\
    - declared output shape and type;\
    - deterministic greedy test behavior where stable;\
    - logits or embeddings within pre-registered tolerance where exposed;\
    - sampled-output evaluation as distributions, not string equality;\
    - backend identity always present in provenance.\
\
Acceptance:\
  - Rust tests under both feature sets.\
  - JSON schema and drift tests.\
  - Swift and Kotlin binding tests.\
  - mutation tests for each load-bearing property.\
  - CI green on exact PR head.\
  - explicit nonclaim: no runtime or model executed.\
