\
This document is the program roadmap, not permission to implement every\
milestone in one uninterrupted branch or pull request.\
\
Execute exactly one milestone at a time.\
\
For each milestone:\
\
1. Verify the repository, branch, clean worktree, and exact base SHA.\
2. Create one dedicated branch.\
3. Implement only that milestone's declared scope.\
4. Run every required local gate.\
5. Regenerate bindings and native artifacts when the contract changes.\
6. Push the branch.\
7. Open or update one pull request.\
8. Wait for exact-head CI.\
9. Address branch-caused CI failures and review findings with minimal,\
   evidence-based changes.\
10. Re-run the complete affected acceptance surface after every fix.\
11. Stop when the milestone reaches an operator-review boundary.\
12. Never merge the pull request.\
13. Never begin the next milestone before the operator merges the current one.\
\
Valid terminal states:\
\
ACHIEVED\
  - all milestone acceptance criteria hold;\
  - exact-head CI is green;\
  - required physical-device evidence is recorded;\
  - the PR resolution summary is posted;\
  - the PR is open and awaiting operator merge.\
\
BLOCKED_OPERATOR\
  - signing, physical interaction, account login, purchase, legal acceptance,\
    secret provisioning, manual UI observation, or merge authority is required.\
\
BLOCKED_EXTERNAL\
  - an upstream service, runner, SDK, model artifact, store review, hardware,\
    or documented platform capability is unavailable.\
\
BLOCKED_EVIDENCE\
  - the requested support or promotion claim cannot be established from the\
    available tests or hardware.\
\
A blocked terminal state must report:\
  - exact branch and head;\
  - completed work;\
  - remaining blocker;\
  - commands or manual action required;\
  - claims that remain explicitly unmade.\
\
Do not broaden scope merely because time or context remains.\
\
Command structure: one /goal per milestone; an optional /loop only while\
waiting on external CI or review state (poll, minimal branch-caused fixes,\
never merge, never start the next milestone).\
